Local mathematical port of DQuickLTFit numerical convolution, copyright(C)2016-2021Danny Petschke, GNU GPLversion3or later; GPL text is in LICENSE. Original numerical oracle used unchanged multiExpDecay and MPFIT-C. The cleaned implementation uses explicit local mathematics and general SciPy Levenberg-Marquardt. Source/data revisions and changes are documented privately in test/validation.md.
Real measurements: Danny Petschke,Ricardo Helm,Torsten E.M.Staab, Data on pure tin by PALS acquired with a semi-analog/digital setup using DDRS4PALS, Data in Brief22(2019),16-29, DOI10.1016/j.dib.2018.11.121. Original paper and data supplement are CC BY4.0; attribution and source DOI retained. Native integer observations were repackaged as NPZ; analysis binning does not modify stored raw data.
